    "text": "To determine the number of lattes sold by the coffee shop, we start by defining the variables and setting up the equation based on the given information.\n\nLet \\( t \\) represent the number of teas sold. According to the problem, the number of lattes sold is 8 more than four times the number of teas sold. Therefore, we can express the number of lattes sold as:\n\\[ l = 4t + 8 \\]\n\nWe are given that 6 teas were sold, so we substitute \\( t = 6 \\) into the equation:\n\\[ l = 4(6) + 8 \\]\n\nNext, we perform the multiplication:\n\\[ l = 24 + 8 \\]\n\nThen, we add the numbers together:\n\\[ l = 32 \\]\n\nThus, the number of lattes sold by the coffee shop is \\(\\boxed{32}\\).",
